<title>GERMANY: German government raises yield on 5-year Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government raises yield on 5-year Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is raising the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds (Bobls) by lowering the issue price of the paper to 99.30 percent from 100.20 percent, the Bundesbank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The move brings the yield on the paper, which is due May 17, 2002, to 4.66 percent from 4.44 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
